($t$Copernicia prunifera$t$, $t$Copernicia prunifera$t$, $t$Arecaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Arecaceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 12 m. Copernicia prunifera or Carnauba Palm is a tropical fan palm native to north eastern Brazil. It grows up to 20 m in height with trunk diameter of up to 25 cm. It has a circular tree crown. The flowers are bisexual. The fruits are round, small, and black. The plant, particularly the coating of the leaves, is a source of carnauba wax which is used to make varnishes, lubricant, soap, candles, etc. The fruit and pith are edible. The pith has high starch content and is used to make sago. The trunk also yields an edible gum. The leaves and the apical bud are both eaten as vegetable. The seed is used as coffee substitute and is a source of oil. The leaves are used as thatching and weaving material. Leaf fibres are made into ropes. The wood is used for fuel, poles, fencing, etc. The plant is drought resistant. Other names include wax palm and carnauba.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Brazilian Wax Palm, Carnauba Palm, Carnauba Wax$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): Plant has spines or sharp edges; use extreme caution when handling$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Arecaceae", "giorni_germinazio